{
  "name": "1940_ioannina",
  "title": "Battle of Ioannina / Pindus, Oct-Nov 1940",
  "notes": "Greco-Italian War, 28 Oct - mid Nov 1940. Rosters rebuilt with real battalion-level names (en/it/el Wikipedia: Battle of Pindus, Greco-Italian War, XXV Army Corps 'Ciamuria', 3rd Alpine Division 'Julia', 51st/23rd/47th Infantry Divisions, 131st Armored Division 'Centauro', 8th Infantry Division (Greece), Konstantinos Davakis, Cavalry Division (Greece), 1st Infantry Division (Greece); Gedeon 2001). Italy invaded from Albania toward Ioannina; direction = NW (Gjirokaster/Kalpaki — the Ciamuria main axis; battle_scan 3914: NW neighbor 914 = the historical Kakavia-Gjirokaster road; the Julia Pindus axis (NE, toward Metsovo) is a separate engagement folded onto this board — a single NW strip keeps T1 gap ~3, the NW+NE double strip spans the whole north edge and strands the lines 8+ hexes apart). Corrections vs the original draft: (1) Julia 1940 = 8 Rgt Alpini (Cividale/Gemona/Tolmezzo) + 9 Rgt (L'Aquila/Vicenza) + Val mobilization bns (Tagliamento/Fella/Natisone/Cismon, November arrivals) + 3 Rgt Art. Alpina (Gr. Conegliano/Udine 75/13) + III Btg. misto Genio — Bassano/Feltre left the division in 1937 (Tridentina/Pusteria) and never fought here; (2) Centauro had NO M13/40 in Oct-Nov 1940 — only I-IV Btg. Carri L (L3/35 tankettes, 163 tanks 90 usable) + 5 Rgt Bersaglieri (XIV/XXII/XXIV) + 131 Rgt Art (M13 battalions arrived Jan 1941); (3) Acqui (33.) reached Albania 18 Dec on the coast — NOT in the battle window, excluded; Bari (47.) arrived 2 Nov (139 Rgt to Konitsa/Perati bridge relieving Julia, 140 Rgt to Leskovik) — included at reduced org; (4) the sole CC.NN in-sector = 82 Legione 'Benito Mussolini' (LXVIII/LXXXII, late Nov, org 40); (5) Greek 8. Div = 10/15/24 Rgt + 3/40 Evzone Rgt (15 bns, 16 batteries — NOT 12/17/22) + 3rd Inf Bde; Pindos Detachment (Davakis ~2,000, 4 guns) = I/II/51 Rgt (III/51 arriving piecemeal) + cavalry troop + mountain battery; 1. Div (Vrachnos: 1/2 Rgt) counterattacked from 1 Nov, Cavalry Division (Stanotas: 3 Cav Rgt + Mech Cav Rgt + 4 Inf Rgt + 7 Rgt bn) and Cavalry Bde (Dimaratos) closed the trap; 2/39 Evzone Rgt (from 4. Div) reinforced the Kalamas. Scale = real battalions: attacker 60 (Julia 13 + Ferrara 12 + Siena 10 + Bari 10 + Centauro 10 + corps 5) vs defender 44 (8. Div 14 + 3rd Bde 2 + Pindos 5 + 1. Div 7 + Cav Div 9 + Cav Bde 2 + 2/39 3 + Epirus det 2) — historical manpower ~55k vs ~35k. Under-strength via org: Italian Siena 50/Ferrara 58/Bari 55, Val bns 50, CC.NN 40, L3 6 (90/163 usable), Greeks 8. Div 58/24 Rgt 50/Pindos 45-40/1. Div 55/Cav 50-55/2/39 55. Terrain: mountain province + 8px river (the Kalamas/Thyamis line — the historical Greek defense line); AI plays guerrilla_tactics (ambush/defend-in-place). Stats = 1939 calibration.",
